<section class="approach">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">My approach</p>
    <h2>You need a coach who's lived it.</h2>
    <p>Coaching has been part of my work for twenty years. Since 2009, I've been a certified executive coach and have coached executive leaders and teams on performance, leadership and navigating change. As part of my work in Learning and Development, I've also taught hundreds of leaders how to coach. More important than the credential, though, is that I've also been where you are. I've held global senior leadership roles, so I understand the pressure from the inside. I'm a woman with a physical disability, which means I've rebuilt a career in a workplace that wasn't built for me. My advanced diploma in coaching with neuroscience grounds the work in how our brains actually respond to stress, how our beliefs shape us, and why our values matter. Whatever you're facing, professional or personal, you don't need a coach who's read about it. You need one who's lived it.</p>
    <p class="credentials"><strong>Diploma in Executive Coaching</strong> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Advanced Diploma in Coaching with Neuroscience</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="how-i-work">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>
    <h2>The work inside the sessions.</h2>
    <p>Coaching is all about helping you find the answers. It's about listening and helping you understand what you are thinking, doing and believing that might be blocking you from achieving your desired outcome.</p>
    <p>I obtained my first executive leadership coaching certificate in 2009, and in 2021 I decided that to be the best coach I could be, I should understand how our brain works. I got an advanced diploma in coaching with neuroscience. Neuroscience in coaching is an evidence-based way of working that looks at how the brain functions, rewires itself and processes emotions. It can help you break away from old patterns and create new, more productive ones. Like taking a new route home after travelling the same one for so long, you can do it with your eyes closed.</p>
    <p>In our sessions, we look at some of these paths you keep travelling and why you stay on them even though they no longer serve you. Together we get to a clearer view of your belief system, your values, and the emotional intelligence shaping how you respond to others.</p>
    <p>Clients walk away, usually after seven to ten sessions, with a clearer sense of why they react a certain way, why they get along with some people and not at all with others, and a stronger grip on how to move toward goals that genuinely align with their values.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="how-section">
  <div class="container how-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who I work with</p>
    <h2>Two practices, same depth.</h2>
    <p>I coach two distinct audiences. Different starting points, the same depth of attention to the work.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tier-section">
  <div class="tier-grid">
    <div>
      <h2>Executive &amp; Career Coaching</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <p class="tier-for">For senior leaders navigating transitions, leading authentically, and figuring out what's next.</p>
      <p>This is where most of my coaching takes place. People stepping into bigger roles, considering a move, leading through change, or working out how to bring more of themselves to their leadership. We work on what's actually in the way: the strategic decisions, the difficult conversations, and the parts of yourself you've been managing rather than leading from.</p>
      <p>Senior career transitions sit here too. Career coaching at this level isn't a different product. It's the same depth of work, often at a moment when the stakes are personal as well as professional.</p>
      <blockquote class="tier-quote">
        <p>"{{ testimonials.coaching_executive.quote }}"</p>
        <cite><strong>{{ testimonials.coaching_executive.name }}</strong> &middot; {{ testimonials.coaching_executive.role }}</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tier-section tier-2">
  <div class="tier-grid">
    <div>
      <h2>Return-to-Work &amp; Confidence Coaching</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <p class="tier-for">For people rebuilding professional momentum after a break.</p>
      <p>Maternity leave, illness, redundancy, caring responsibilities, life. Whatever pulled you out of work, getting back in takes more than an updated CV. We work on both the practical (CV, applications, interviews, networks) and the underneath (the inner critic, the confidence rebuild, the story you tell yourself about who you are now).</p>
      <p>If you're returning at any level and need someone who'll meet the work with both honesty and warmth, this is for you.</p>
      <blockquote class="tier-quote">
        <p>"{{ testimonials.coaching_return_to_work.quote }}"</p>
        <cite><strong>{{ testimonials.coaching_return_to_work.name }}</strong> &middot; {{ testimonials.coaching_return_to_work.role }}</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="book-section" id="book">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--gold)">First step</p>
    <h2>A free 30-minute chemistry chat.</h2>
    <p>We'll talk about where you are, where you're trying to get to, and whether I'm the right person to help. No prep needed. If we're a fit, we agree how to start. If we're not, I'll point you in the right direction.</p>
    <div class="book-cta-row">
      <a href="https://calendly.com/hello-iamphoenix/30min" onclick="Calendly.initPopupWidget({url: 'https://calendly.com/hello-iamphoenix/30min'});return false;" class="btn-primary">Book a chemistry chat</a>
